WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.000
GROUP BY, WHERE and HAVING
WHERE filters individual rows before grouping. GROUP BY combines equal values. HAVING checks aggregates of completed groups.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Explanation
SUM(amount) totals each group. Example data: city A has 100 and 150; city B has 80. HAVING keeps only totals above 200.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Trace the code
-- sales(city, amount): (A,100), (A,150), (B,80)
SELECT city, SUM(amount) AS total
FROM sales
GROUP BY city
HAVING SUM(amount) > 200;

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Result
A 250

A: 100+150=250 passes; B:80 does not.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Remember
Do not confuse row count with total amount: COUNT(*) counts rows and SUM(amount) adds values. Here you trace the result without a live database.
